    "created_at": "2018-01-09T21:09:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-09T21:09:24Z",
    "body": "I agree with Domenic.  In the case of HTMLCanvasElement.toBlob, throwing an exception might be a bit too harsh because it interrupts JS execution if not caught. In cases where errors can happen in situations that are hard to foresee/repro for web developers (e.g. canvas pixels failed to allocate on low RAM device), it is arguably better if APIs fail silently rather than throw.\r\n\r\nFor promise-based APIs however, rejecting with an exception gives the best of both worlds.  The code will fail gracefully even if call site does not explicitly handle rejects.",
